1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:08,688
Welcome to Visual Fashion Product Search, a graduation project at
the International University of Technology Twintech.

2
00:00:09,008 --> 00:00:14,802
The project is developed by Nasser Yousef, Noor Yousef, and Naeem
Basalma,

3
00:00:14,802 --> 00:00:17,216
supervised by Doctor Ayman Alsabri.

4
00:00:18,986 --> 00:00:24,274
Finding clothing with words can be difficult when a user does not
know the product name.

5
00:00:24,594 --> 00:00:30,488
Our application accepts an image and retrieves visually similar
clothing from a local catalogue.

6
00:00:30,808 --> 00:00:37,121
The original gallery contains three thousand and sixty-eight images
across ten clothing categories.

7
00:00:38,891 --> 00:00:43,385
First, upload a photograph and choose full-image search.

8
00:00:43,705 --> 00:00:51,463
The system prepares the image, extracts a visual representation, and
ranks catalogue images by similarity.

9
00:00:51,783 --> 00:00:55,379
A photograph containing several garments may describe the whole
scene

10
00:00:55,379 --> 00:00:58,616
instead of the item the user intends to find.

11
00:01:00,386 --> 00:01:05,769
To focus the query, choose intelligent selection and click the
intended garment.

12
00:01:06,089 --> 00:01:12,852
SAM2.1 generates a mask. Positive and negative points help refine
the selection.

13
00:01:13,172 --> 00:01:18,376
Review the cutout before accepting it, then search using the
selected garment.

14
00:01:18,696 --> 00:01:23,322
The results show visually similar catalogue items. Similarity scores

15
00:01:23,322 --> 00:01:27,434
are not probabilities of an exact commercial-product match.

16
00:01:29,204 --> 00:01:33,082
The browser communicates with a FastAPI backend.

17
00:01:33,402 --> 00:01:39,075
SigLIP2 produces a normalized vector with seven hundred and sixty-
eight dimensions.

18
00:01:39,395 --> 00:01:43,766
FAISS ranks the vectors. Both full images

19
00:01:43,766 --> 00:01:47,738
and accepted garment cutouts pass through the same visual encoder.

20
00:01:48,058 --> 00:01:52,875
The models run locally, using a compatible graphics processor when
available,

21
00:01:52,875 --> 00:01:55,502
with a CPU fallback.

22
00:01:57,272 --> 00:02:01,447
On one hundred historical synthetic queries containing multiple
garments,

23
00:02:01,447 --> 00:02:05,623
category correctness at the first result increased from forty-six

24
00:02:05,623 --> 00:02:09,799
percent for full images to seventy-five percent after selection.

25
00:02:10,119 --> 00:02:13,628
This is a gain of twenty-nine percentage points.

26
00:02:13,948 --> 00:02:17,311
It measures category relevance under that experiment,

27
00:02:17,311 --> 00:02:22,115
rather than general accuracy for identifying the exact commercial
product.

28
00:02:23,885 --> 00:02:28,187
A protected local administrator can add, edit, and delete products,

29
00:02:28,187 --> 00:02:31,628
with up to five photographs for each product.

30
00:02:31,948 --> 00:02:38,162
Product details include category, optional price and currency, and
availability.

31
00:02:38,482 --> 00:02:43,130
Guests can search these added products from the main page without an
account.

32
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:47,509
Backup and restore tools help preserve the added catalogue.

33
00:02:49,279 --> 00:02:53,828
The current system supports local visual search and product
management.

34
00:02:54,148 --> 00:02:58,038
The original image index remains active because cropping catalogue

35
00:02:58,038 --> 00:03:01,496
images did not show a sufficient consistent improvement.

36
00:03:01,816 --> 00:03:08,824
The next research priority is a larger set of verified product
identities and independent query photographs.

37
00:03:10,594 --> 00:03:18,612
The public GitHub repository provides the source code, editable
documentation, and instructions for the runtime resources.

38
00:03:18,932 --> 00:03:20,946
Thank you for watching.
